-- title:
--   Coarse moduli at raised level ℓ from a line-stabiliser quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $q\neq q'$ be primes and $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ such that `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'` holds, i.e. $a>0$ or $b>0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of the integers of $\mathbb Q$ the algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible exactly when $q\in v$ or $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda\subseteq\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ be a maximal order (an order containing no strictly larger order), let $N,m\in\mathbb N$, and let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring in which $N$ and $m$ are units. Let $\pi_M\colon M\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ carry a fine moduli structure `ptF` for pairs (fake elliptic curve with $\Lambda$-action and level $N$, full level-$m$ structure) over $\mathcal O$-rings, and let a finite group $G$ act through $\rho$ on $M$ with labels $\chi\colon G\to\Lambda$ realising level twisting (`IsLevelTwistAction`). Let $\pi\colon M\to X$ over $\mathcal O$ and a rule `pt` make $X$ a coarse moduli scheme for fake elliptic curves of level $N$, with $\mathrm{pt}(E)=\mathrm{ptF}(E,P)$ followed by $\pi$ on pairs. Let $\ell$ be a prime dividing $m$ and $L_0\subseteq\Lambda$ a left $\Lambda$-submodule with $\ell\Lambda\subseteq L_0$ and relative index $\ell^2$ in $\Lambda$, and let $H\le G$ consist exactly of those $g$ with $L_0\chi(g)\subseteq L_0$. Let $\pi_H\colon M\to X_H$ over $\mathcal O$ be an $H$-quotient: invariant under each $\rho h$, integral, affine, surjective on points, with fibres of $\pi_H$ on points the $H$-orbits, injective sheaf maps whose image on each open is the $H$-invariants, with $H$-stable affine opens of $M$ arising as preimages of affine opens, and universal among $H$-invariant morphisms; and let $d_0\colon X_H\to X$ satisfy $\pi_H$ followed by $d_0$ equals $\pi$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an open $U\subseteq X_H$ and a rule `ptT` sending each $(E,K)$ with $K$ an extra level at $\ell$ to a point of $U$ over $\mathcal O$ such that: $U$ is also closed in $X_H$; $(U,\;U.\iota\gg\pi_{XH},\;\mathrm{ptT})$ is a coarse moduli scheme for pairs (fake elliptic curve of level $N$, extra level at $\ell$) in the sense of `IsCoarseModuliT`; whenever $K$ is geometrically characterised by the line $L_0\cdot(m/\ell)P$, that is, for all algebraically closed $k$, all $S\to k$ and all points $Q$ over the resulting geometric point, $Q$ factors through $K$'s immersion iff $Q=x_*\big((m/\ell)\cdot P\big)$ for some $x\in\Lambda$ with $x\in L_0$, then $\mathrm{ptT}(E,K)$ followed by $U.\iota$ equals $\mathrm{ptF}(E,P)$ followed by $\pi_H$; $\mathrm{ptT}(v)$ followed by $U.\iota$ and $d_0$ equals $\mathrm{pt}$ of the underlying curve; for algebraically closed $k'$ and a full-level pair $u$ over $k'$, the image under $\pi_H$ of the fine point of $u$ at the closed point lies in $U$ iff some extra level at $\ell$ is characterised by the same line $L_0\cdot(m/\ell)P$; and $U=\top$ when $\ell\nmid N$.
--
--   This is the level-raising step for the quaternionic (Shimura-curve) moduli problem: passing from the fine moduli scheme at full level $m$ to a coarse moduli scheme for $\Gamma_0(\ell)$-type data, realised as a clopen piece of the quotient of $M$ by the stabiliser of a $\Lambda$-line $L_0\subseteq\Lambda/\ell\Lambda$, the clopen condition recording that the line generated by $L_0\cdot(m/\ell)P$ meets the level-$N$ structure trivially. It feeds the subsequent base-change, integrality and properness statements for these coarse moduli schemes.
